prompt:
Write a Java method that takes a string parameter, processes it according to the following rules, and returns its MD5 hash using a standard library function:

1. The input string must be trimmed and must not exceed 1024 characters in length.
2. If the input is null, throw a custom exception `InvalidInputException` with an appropriate message.
3. The method should handle any exceptions that occur during the hashing process and log them without crashing the application.
4. Implement a performance optimization by caching previously computed MD5 hashes for the first 10 unique strings processed.
5. Ensure thread safety when accessing the cache.
6. The method should be able to handle concurrent requests efficiently.

```java
public class HashProcessor {
    private static final int CACHE_SIZE = 10;
    private static final Map<String, String> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final Set<String> processedStrings = Collections.synchronizedSet(new HashSet<>());

    public static String computeMD5Hash(String input) throws InvalidInputException {
        if (input == null) {
            throw new InvalidInputException("Input cannot be null.");
        }
        input = input.trim();
        if (input.length() > 1024) {
            throw new InvalidInputException("Input exceeds maximum length of 1024 characters.");
        }

        try {
            synchronized (processedStrings) {
                if (processedStrings.contains(input)) {
                    return cache.get(input);
                }
                processedStrings.add(input);

                if (cache.size() >= CACHE_SIZE) {
                    cache.clear();
                }

                String hash = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5").update(input.getBytes()).digest().toString();
                cache.put(input, hash);
                return hash;
            }
        } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            logException(e);
            throw new RuntimeException("MD5 algorithm not found.", e);
        }
    }

    private static void logException(Exception e) {
        // Log the exception details for debugging purposes.
    }

    public static class InvalidInputException extends Exception {
        public InvalidInputException(String message) {
            super(message);
        }
    }
}
```

