The `TaskQueue` class manages the task queue using a thread-safe approach with mutexes and condition variables. Tasks are enqueued and dequeued by worker threads, which execute tasks asynchronously. The `TaskProcessor` class coordinates the creation of worker threads and starts processing tasks.

The program includes signal handling to gracefully shut down all active tasks when a termination signal is received (e.g., Ctrl+C).

To fully implement the task queue system with custom task types, prioritization, multiple queues, configuration file support, logging, memory efficiency, resilience, stress testing, robustness, and unit tests, additional code and configurations would need to be added.']

